'''Original''' ({{lang|ca|Original}}) is the historic centre and administrative heart of [[Sant Cristòfor]], the capital city of [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. With a population of 731,320 across 83.35 km², it is the second-most populous of Sant Cristòfor's eleven [[ciutats of Sant Cristòfor|ciutats]] after [[Barcelona (ciutat)|Barcelona]]. Original occupies the eastern shore of the [[Badia de Sant Cristòfor]], stretching from the working-class southern neighbourhoods along the bay's head to the wealthy hillside barris in the north. It is home to the [[National Assembly of Balboa|National Assembly]], the [[Borsa de Sant Cristòfor]], the [[Grand Train Terminal|Estació Gran]], and the city's principal ferry terminal.

Original is the oldest part of Sant Cristòfor, founded in 1524 as the Volisanian colonial settlement on the bay shore. Its street pattern still reflects the layered history of the city: the narrow medieval lanes of [[El Raval]] and [[La Tanneria]] in the south, the grid extensions of [[L'Eixample Sud]] and [[L'Eixample Est]] from the nineteenth and early twentieth centuries, the Zong-era [[Fosian Balboan|Fosian]] cultural quarter around [[Turó del Temple]] and [[Barri del Te]], and the modern skyscrapers of [[El Centre]], the [[Districte Financer]], and [[Plaça Major]] along the bay waterfront.

== Geography ==

Original occupies the eastern shore of the [[Badia de Sant Cristòfor]], the U-shaped bay that defines the geography of Sant Cristòfor. The ciutat extends roughly 12 km from north to south and 5–8 km from east to west, bounded by the bay to the west, the [[Serralada d'Estret]] foothills to the east, and the neighbouring ciutats of [[Costa Nord (ciutat)|Costa Nord]] to the north, [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]] and [[Sant Martí (ciutat)|Sant Martí]] to the east, and [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]] to the south.

The terrain rises gently from the bay shore eastward toward the foothills. The waterfront barris — [[La Seu]], [[La Universitat]], [[La Diagonal]], [[Molls Superiors]], [[Molls Inferiors]], [[El Centre]], the [[Districte Financer]], and [[Plaça Major]] — occupy the narrow coastal strip along the bay, with elevations generally below 20 metres. The central and eastern barris — [[L'Eixample Est]], [[La Verneda]], [[Barri dels Teatres]] — sit on slightly higher ground, 30–60 metres above sea level. The northern barris — [[Sant Gervasi]], [[Les Vil·les]], [[La Seu]] — begin to climb into the lower Serralada foothills, reaching elevations of 80–120 metres.

The [[Riu Llobregat]] enters the bay near the northern boundary of Original, forming a small delta at its mouth. Several smaller ''rieres'' (streams) drain from the hills across the ciutat, though most have been culverted or channelised through the urban area.

