== Transport ==

{{main|Metro de Sant Cristòfor|Transport in Sant Cristòfor}}

Original is the transport hub of Sant Cristòfor. Seven of the city's nine metro lines converge in the ciutat, and the [[Grand Train Terminal|Estació Gran]] at [[Plaça Major]] is the western terminus of the [[Isthmus Railway]].

=== Metro ===

{{main|Metro de Sant Cristòfor}}

Seven of the city's nine metro lines serve Original (Lines 1–7). Line 8 clips the southeast corner only; Line 9 does not serve the ciutat. There are approximately 50 stations in Original, including several major interchange hubs.

The principal metro hubs in Original are:

* '''[[Districte Financer]]''' — 4 lines (L3, L4, L5, L7); the city's busiest interchange
* '''[[Plaça Major]]''' — 3 lines (L3, L5, L7); adjacent to the Estació Gran
* '''[[Estació Gran]]''' — Lines 1 and 2; the Grand Train Terminal, western terminus of the Isthmus Railway
* '''[[La Diagonal]]''' — 3 lines (L3, L5, L7); luxury shopping and museum district
* '''[[Molls Superiors]]''' — 3 lines (L3, L5, L7); waterfront interchange
* '''[[L'Eixample Sud]]''' — 3 lines (L3, L4, L7); southern interchange

Three barris — [[El Centre]], [[La Sagrada]], and [[Les Vil·les]] — have no metro station and are served by the streetcar and bus networks.

=== Streetcar ===

{{main|Tramvia de Sant Cristòfor}}

Four streetcar lines radiate from the Estació Gran through the narrow streets of the historic core, providing last-mile connections where metro stations are too far apart:

* '''T1''': Estació Gran → bay shore → financial district → southern neighbourhoods
* '''T2''': Estació Gran → eastern boulevard → Dàrsena border
* '''T3''': Estació Gran → northern boulevard → Costa Nord border
* '''T4''': Estació Gran → western boulevard → Sant Jordi border

=== Ferry ===

{{main|Ferries de la Badia de Sant Cristòfor}}

The [[Sant Cristòfor Main ferry terminal]] in [[Molls Inferiors]] is the principal mainland ferry terminal, providing connections to [[Pandao]] (Barcelona), [[Illa del Portal]], [[Costa Nord]], and [[Daurada]].

=== Rail ===

The [[Grand Train Terminal|Estació Gran de Sant Cristòfor]] at [[Plaça Major]] is the western terminus of the [[Isthmus Railway]] and the principal long-distance and commuter rail station in Sant Cristòfor.

== Economy ==

Original is the financial and governmental centre of Balboa. The [[Districte Financer]] houses the [[Borsa de Sant Cristòfor]] (the national stock exchange), the headquarters of most major Balboan banks, and the regional offices of international firms. The [[National Assembly of Balboa|National Assembly]] sits in [[Plaça Major]], and most government ministries have their headquarters in the waterfront barris.

The ciutat's economy is dominated by financial services, government, professional services, and tourism. The [[Mercat Plaça]] market is one of the largest traditional markets in Abyala. The [[Districte Càrnic]] and [[Districte Càrnic Sud]] remain active meatpacking districts, a rare surviving industrial zone in the increasingly service-oriented ciutat.

== Education ==

Original is home to two major universities:

* The '''[[Universitat de Sant Cristòfor]]''' in [[La Universitat]] — the largest university in Balboa, founded in 1871
* The '''[[Balboan Jesuit University]]''' in [[La Seu]] — a private Catholic university, founded in 1903

== Culture ==

Original's cultural life is concentrated in several distinct quarters:

* The '''theatre district''' in [[Barri dels Teatres]] — the city's principal entertainment zone, with large dining halls, theatres, and Zong/Sinchewse cultural venues
* The '''tea quarter''' in [[Barri del Te]] — famous for its traditional teahouses, Zong galleries, publishing houses, and media studios
* The '''Nakamian cultural heart''' in [[Petit Nakamizu]] — Kairyū Buddhist temples, Nakamian shops, ''balboazushi'' restaurants, and the annual Nakamian Cultural Parade
* The '''market culture''' of [[Mercat Plaça]] — the city's principal traditional market, with Birú traders, food stalls, and open-air commerce
* The '''museum strip''' along [[La Diagonal]] — high-end museums, galleries, and cultural institutions on the bay waterfront

